  "strengthened_criterion": {
    "proved": true,
    "theorem": "If mult(\u03bb\u2082(P\u2299P))\u2265d and \u2211_{ijkl}M_ijkl\u00b2 \u2264 Wick_hi = 12n\u00b2+48n, then for every prime p\u22655 one has \u2211M\u00b2\u2264thr_gap=4d\u00b2(d+4) (Prop 15.95.1), hence by Prop 15.94 gap criterion \u03bb\u2082\u2264\u221a(Q/d)\u2264d/(2N), hence bi-tight covers are empty (Prop 15.55\u201315.56). Q=Tr((P\u2299P)\u00b2)\u2212\u03b1\u00b2=\u2211M\u00b2/(16N\u00b2)\u2212d\u00b2/N\u00b2, \u03b1=d/N.",
    "open_inputs": "Need mult(\u03bb\u2082)\u2265d and \u2211M\u00b2\u2264Wick_hi for all primes p\u22655. Both certified at p=5,7; mult=d also at p=3 (gap fails via thr)."
  },
